REJECTED: CSP pattern hit in an added line :: /style\s*=/  (x7)
Root cause: touching an existing line that already carried a pre-existing
`style="..."` attribute to insert `for="id"`/`aria-label="..."` re-emits
that line's whole content as "added" in the diff, which the CSP
Added-Lines Gate cannot distinguish from a genuinely NEW inline style.
Fix: reverted the 7 affected template-string lines to their original,
untouched text and wired the for=/aria-label attributes via a
post-render DOM pass instead (querySelector + setAttribute), which adds
new lines containing no `style=` substring rather than modifying the
existing ones. Re-ran the full suite after the fix — unchanged, still
196/196 passing, tsc/build still clean.

